{"id":"civicplus-4-01132026-4420","platform":"civicplus","body":"Planning Commission","name":"2026 01 13 Special January PC Meeting Agenda Page","date":"2026-01-13","time":"","canceled":false,"agenda_url":"https://www.cityofinglewood.org/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_01132026-4420","minutes_url":"https://www.cityofinglewood.org/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Minutes/_01132026-4420","packet_url":"","category_id":4,"agenda_text":"CITY OF INGLEWOOD\n  DEVELOPMENT SERVICES DEPARTMENT\n  PLANNING DIVISION\n  SPECIAL PLANNING COMMISSION MEETING AGENDA\nJanuary 13, 2026, 7:00 P.M.\nCity Council Chambers – Ninth Floor\n1 West Manchester Boulevard\n\n1.  Pledge of Allegiance.\n\n2.  Roll Call.\n\n3.  Communications from staff.\n\n4.  Public Comments Regarding Agenda Items. Persons wishing to address\n  the Planning Commission on any item on the agenda other than a\n  public hearing may do so at this time.\n\n5.  PUBLIC HEARING:\n  a. A public hearing to consider Zoning Code Amendment No. 25-00002\n  (ZCA25-00002) to modify miscellaneous regulations in Chapter 12 of\n  the Inglewood Municipal Code (IMC) related to Public Hearing Notice\n  Requirements, Planned Assembly Development Requirements, Removal\n  of the Art Deco Design Standards, and Cosmetology Uses, Citywide.\n\n  A Notice of Exemption (EA-CE-2026-004) has been prepared stating\n  that the proposed project is exempt from the California\n  Environmental Quality Act (CEQA), a copy of which is available for\n  public review in the Planning Division office of City Hall and via\n  email at rbrooks@cityofinglewood.org.\n\n  Preliminary Recommendations:\n  A. If the Planning Commission determines to RECOMMEND the\n  request, it is recommended to:\n  1)Affirm the categorical exemption EA-CE-2026-004;\n  2)Adopt the resolution approving ZCA25-00002.\n  B. If the Planning Commission determines to ADD REGULATIONS, it is\n  recommended to:\n  1)Take the above actions but modify the number of conditions\n  as appropriate.\n  C. If the Planning Commission determines to recommend DENIAL of\n  the Code Amendment or any part thereof, it is recommended to:\n  1)Take the appropriate actions and make the findings.\n  Item 5a Documents\n\n6.  NON-PUBLIC HEARINGS:\n  a. A non-public hearing to consider an application by Dylan Moyana,\n  representing  Costco  Wholesale  Corporation,  to  allow  an\n  approximately 3,000 square-foot addition to an existing 149,700\n  square-foot commercial building on an approximately 15.7-acre M-1L\n  (Limited Manufacturing) zoned property at 3560 West Century\n  Boulevard.\n\n  A Notice of Exemption (EA-CE-2026-001) has been prepared stating\n  that the proposed project is categorically exempt from the\n  California Environmental Quality Act, a copy of which is available\n  for public review in the Planning Division office of City Hall and\n  via email request to al-martell@cityofinglewood.org.\n\n  Preliminary Recommendations:\n  A. If the Planning Commission determines to APPROVE the request,\n  it is recommended to:\n  1) Affirm the Categorical Exemption EA-CE-2026-001;\n  2) Adopt the resolution approving DR25-00061.\n  B. If the Planning Commission determines to ADD CONDITIONS, it is\n  recommended to:\n\f  1) Take the above actions but modify the number of conditions\n  as appropriate.\n  C. If the Planning Commission determines to DENY the request or\n  any part thereof, it is recommended to:\n  1) Take the appropriate actions and make the findings.\n  Item 6a Documents\n\n7.  Public Comments. Anyone wishing to address the Planning Commission\n  on any matter within their jurisdiction and not elsewhere\n  considered on the agenda may do so at this time.\n\n8.  Commission Initiatives.\n\n9.  Adjournment.\n\nIf you will require special accommodations, due to a disability, please\ncontact the Planning Division at (310) 412-5230, One Manchester\nBoulevard, Fourth Floor, Inglewood City Hall, Inglewood, CA 90301. All\nrequests for special accommodations must be received 48 hours prior to\nthe day of the hearing(s).\n\n\"Si no entiende esta noticia o si necesita más información, favor de\nllamar a este número (310) 412-5230.\"\n\nIn the event that the Planning Commission meeting of January 13, 2026,\nis not held, or is concluded prior to a public hearing or other agenda\nitem being considered, the public hearing or non-public hearing agenda\nitem will automatically be continued to the next regular Planning\nCommission meeting.\n\n  NEXT PLANNING COMMISSION MEETING:\n  WEDNESDAY, FEBRUARY 4, 7:00 P.M.\n  CITY COUNCIL CHAMBERS, NINTH FLOOR, INGLEWOOD CITY HALL\n  ONE MANCHESTER BOULEVARD\n  INGLEWOOD, CA 90301\n\n  2","minutes_text":"PK\u0003\u0004\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000;\u001c\u000b��\u0001\u0000\u0000*\b\u0000\u0000\u0013\u0000\b\u0002[Content_Types].xml �\u0004\u0002(�\u0000\u0002\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\